1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,946
This is a recorded screenshot walkthrough with synthetic narration. A convincing claim can

2
00:00:05,946 --> 00:00:11,892
leave a person with an unresolved question: what does this finding actually establish,

3
00:00:11,892 --> 00:00:17,838
and what should I ask at my next discussion? EvidenceLoop connects that question

4
00:00:17,838 --> 00:00:23,783
to its source and keeps the context available when the person returns. Our

5
00:00:23,783 --> 00:00:26,985
focus is Healthcare Challenge 2: long-term self-care.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,808
This is a working local engineering prototype. The demonstration uses a fictional fern

7
00:00:35,808 --> 00:00:41,616
study, and replay is visibly labeled. It is not a health recommendation or

8
00:00:41,616 --> 00:00:47,424
a live model response. We chose this example so you can inspect the

9
00:00:47,424 --> 00:00:52,786
behavior without confusing an unfinished clinical evidence library with approved medical advice.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,991
First, the user checks what the claim means. The fictional study describes glow

11
00:01:00,991 --> 00:01:06,983
water, fern height, seven days and a plain-water comparison. The user's intention is

12
00:01:06,983 --> 00:01:12,974
separate from the words of the claim. Confirmation records the meaning to assess;

13
00:01:12,974 --> 00:01:18,966
it does not make the claim true. Unstated information can remain unknown instead

14
00:01:18,966 --> 00:01:21,270
of becoming an invented detail.

15
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,927
The receipt keeps the source and its limits inspectable. A finding about one

16
00:01:40,927 --> 00:01:46,855
outcome in one setting does not establish a guarantee for every situation. The

17
00:01:46,855 --> 00:01:52,782
interface separates the evidence relationship, coverage and intended action. These are bounded demonstration

18
00:01:52,782 --> 00:01:58,709
results. A source passage can show where a statement came from; it cannot

19
00:01:58,709 --> 00:02:03,725
by itself prove that every inference or personal action is justified.

20
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,850
The next step is an exact question the user can preview. Saving is

21
00:02:20,850 --> 00:02:26,700
a separate choice. The screen explains what will be retained, and the save

22
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:32,550
button requires consent. The original pasted text is not stored with the saved

23
00:02:32,550 --> 00:02:38,399
record. Now we simulate a later visit. The person chooses to record that

24
00:02:38,399 --> 00:02:44,249
they discussed the question. This is labeled a self-report, not verified adherence, improved

25
00:02:44,249 --> 00:02:46,499
understanding or a health outcome.

26
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,111
A saved answer must not quietly preserve authority after its evidence changes. These

27
00:03:06,111 --> 00:03:12,221
captures show the result of withdrawing a fictional source. When the user reopens

28
00:03:12,221 --> 00:03:18,332
the saved receipt, the application checks current source status again. The historical record

29
00:03:18,332 --> 00:03:24,443
remains inspectable, but the withdrawn dependency blocks relevant new use. This is a

30
00:03:24,443 --> 00:03:30,554
synthetic withdrawal exercise, not a real publisher correction or a claim that we

31
00:03:30,554 --> 00:03:32,434
automatically monitor medical literature.

32
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:51,559
Ambiguous input should not produce confident advice. This fictional sentence does not identify

33
00:03:51,559 --> 00:03:58,119
the people, intervention or outcome. The user can clarify what they mean, or

34
00:03:58,119 --> 00:04:04,678
leave it unresolved. The application shows its limits. Our live reader remains disabled

35
00:04:04,678 --> 00:04:11,237
because no tested model has passed qualification, so this screen is manual fallback,

36
00:04:11,237 --> 00:04:13,760
not a staged AI success.

37
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:22,571
React presents the workflow, FastAPI enforces policy and versions, and PostgreSQL stores consented

38
00:04:22,571 --> 00:04:29,883
records and separate evidence-review history. Before save, drafts live in expiring server memory.

39
00:04:29,883 --> 00:04:37,194
The optional model can propose structure, but it cannot approve evidence or authorize

40
00:04:37,194 --> 00:04:44,505
a write. The application checks quotes, schemas, ownership, consent and current evidence. A

41
00:04:44,505 --> 00:04:51,816
local single-process design keeps the prototype small; it does not provide production hosting

42
00:04:51,816 --> 00:04:53,503
or cross-device recovery.

43
00:04:55,260 --> 00:05:02,264
WorkBuddy contributed genuine development review. Its Hy3 model examined consent and source-withdrawal code

44
00:05:02,264 --> 00:05:09,269
and proposed missing negative tests. Codex corrected and implemented the proposals and ran

45
00:05:09,269 --> 00:05:16,273
the local checks: forty-four related tests passed. These captures record the contribution and

46
00:05:16,273 --> 00:05:22,200
corrections. WorkBuddy did not run the tests or provide clinical approval.

47
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:31,759
The evidence is deliberately specific. At the October thirteenth checkpoint, the Python suite

48
00:05:31,759 --> 00:05:38,258
passed four hundred ninety-nine tests plus fifty-one subtests. At that checkpoint, a reader

49
00:05:38,258 --> 00:05:44,756
probe matched ten of twelve known regression cases and still failed qualification. We

50
00:05:44,756 --> 00:05:51,255
have no clinical validation or measured health benefit. EvidenceLoop demonstrates a way to

51
00:05:51,255 --> 00:05:57,754
keep meaning, consent and changing evidence connected. The next proof is reliable reading,

52
00:05:57,754 --> 00:06:02,253
independent source review and observed use with fictional tasks.
